{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}-4x$ at  $(1,0)$ intersects the $y$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}-4x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}-4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{1/2}-4x) \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=2(1)^{-1/2}-4=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(0) & =-2(x-1) \\\\ y & =-2x+2-0 \\\\ y & =-2x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2(0)+2=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ed22dab53ddc0c3a22eacd06c63a11fe204e34fd0e80109d2c778d2cee4dee4"} {"question" "q-10830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(0,-1)"] ["math" "(0,-2)"] ["math" "(0,0)"] ["math" "(0,1)"] ["math" "(0,2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-x$ at the point $(1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}-x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-12{x}^{-4}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=-12(1)^{-4}-1=-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-13$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,3),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(3) & =-13(x-1) \\\\ y & =-13x+13+3 \\\\ y & =-13x+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ed22dab53ddc0c3a22eacd06c63a11fe204e34fd0e80109d2c778d2cee4dee4"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-13x"] ["math" "y=-13x+16"] ["math" "y=-13x-16"] ["math" "y=13x"] ["math" "y=13x+16"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-10832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-13x+16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-304068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(-1,-1).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-304068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3x+2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3}{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{-2}-4{x}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(-1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =-\\frac{3}{(-1)^{2}}-\\frac{4}{(-1)^{3}} \\\\  & =-3+4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=1$ and the coordinates of our point $(-1,-1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-1) & =1\\cdot (x-(-1)) \\\\ y+1 & =x+1 \\\\ y & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-304068" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ed22dab53ddc0c3a22eacd06c63a11fe204e34fd0e80109d2c778d2cee4dee4"} {"question" "q-304068" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-304068" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=2x-{x}^{3}$ at the point  $(1,1).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=2x-{x}^{3}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2-3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(1)=2-3({1}^{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-1$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,1),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =(-1)(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1+1 \\\\ y & =-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ed22dab53ddc0c3a22eacd06c63a11fe204e34fd0e80109d2c778d2cee4dee4"} {"question" "q-342350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342350" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point  $(4,-4)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)=-2\\sqrt{x}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y+4 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)-2 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ed22dab53ddc0c3a22eacd06c63a11fe204e34fd0e80109d2c778d2cee4dee4"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"} {"question" "q-342380" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039842/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f6512c6f7178f1d7f8465818cf1ceb5616bc56003f0c8e7390f8c5b00405a0b"}] "usage" {"q-10832" []} "basis" 1382 "retractions" [[17592186092453 :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = \\frac{4}{x^{3}} - x$ at the point $(1, 3)$."] [17592186092453 :question/worked-solution "Differentiate $f(x)=4x^{-3}-x$ to get $f'(x)=-12x^{-4}-1$. At $x=1$, the slope is $-13$. Use the point $(1,3)$:\n$$y-3=-13(x-1),\\qquad y=-13x+16.$$"] [17592186092453 :question/difficulty 17592186045465]] "immutable_answers" [17592186089155 17592186089156 17592186089157 17592186089158